Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once before/after all tests in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost:5000") };
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetOrders_ReturnsOk() { /* ... */ }
}
```

*(These must be `static`.)*

## 3. Once before/after the entire assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start WireMock
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stop WireMock
    }
}
```

## 4. Once for the whole test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseHook
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task Migrate(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.ApplyAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

**Quick-reference summary:**

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, in any class) for a *global* cross-cutting hook that fires for every test in the entire run — handy for logging or timing without touching each test class.
